{
 "id": "sd-webshop-stock-truth",
 "name": "SD: a web shop's stock and backlog: the truth",
 "description": "Tests effects on both sides of the shelf. Picking slows when the shelves run low (a linear effect of the stock on the shelves, normal 300 items, at most 1: pickers cannot pick what is not there), and every order shipped books one item out of stock (a co-flow). The buyer reorders toward 550 items on the shelf, faster the bigger the backlog of customer orders waiting to be picked (a table effect that saturates). The supplier dispatches open purchase orders in about three days, and the goods then spend about a week on the road (a stock the shop does not see) before they reach the shelves. Demand changes without being announced.",
 "time_unit": "day",
